                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Yes, it is as bad as the negative reviews say. Possibly even worse, but you may not ever realize it unless you're a fan of the series. (All caps means this one, regular text means the first game.)\n\nThe -very valid- grief fans have with this game is that THIEF took away most of what made it unique in favor of becoming another watered down dime-a-dozen games. The spacious, open levels were collapsed into narrow critical-path corridors to follow with minor dead end side paths. The story devolved to interpersonal slop instead of revolving around stealing. And your freedom to do whatever your clever mind can think of got confined to item prompt areas. Really the only thing they kept from the originals was light/darkness and sound mechanics. But aside from that you are handheld everywhere you go because god forbid you try and figure things out...\n\nThe unique beauty of Thief games was you not being some dark-tight wearing edgelord wannabe. You were a guy who had to use his wits to figure out even the level itself. Your maps could be anything from blueprints to vague drawings and guesses where you must orient yourself in the location and listen in in order to even figure out where you're supposed to go. And on a stroll over while you're getting your bearings you might hear of something stashed somewhere and your Thief neurons just launch and you tell yourself \"A small detour wouldn't hurt...\" which is glorious emergent gameplay. In THIEF you have pretty much none of that and that is what's heartbreaking and why this game doesn't reach the ankles of the original Thief games.\n\nIf you want to truly immerse yourself in the shoes of the ACTUAL Garret and the ACTUAL Master Thief I urge you to go play Thief 3: Deadly Shadows or even Thief 2: The Metal Age and Thief Gold if you don't mind very old games. All I can say is that if you enjoy immersive and stealth games that aren't about killing, you will likely see the watered down mockery to the Thief franchise Eidos has created here.",
